hadiths[41]{hadithnumber,text}:
"993","On the authority of Hazrat Ibn Mas'ud, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \A Muslim man who testifies that there is no god but Allah and that I (Muhammad"," peace and blessings be upon him) am the Messenger of Allah"," then it is not permissible and permissible to kill him except in three cases: a married adulterer"," a life for a life"," and a person who abandons his religion and separates from the community (of Muslims).\"" (Bukhari and Muslim)"""
"994","It is narrated from Hazrat Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “It is not permissible to kill a Muslim man except in one of three cases: A married adulterer.” He will be stoned to death. (Second) A man who intentionally kills a Muslim will be killed. And (third) the man who leaves the circle of Islam and starts fighting against Allah and His Messenger, he will be killed or executed or exiled."
"995","On the authority of Hazrat Abdullah bin Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \The first cases that will be decided between people on the Day of Resurrection will be cases of blood.\"" (Bukhari and Muslim)."""
"996","Hazrat Samura (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Whoever kills his slave, we will kill him. And whoever cuts off any part of him, we will cut off that part of him.\ (It was narrated by Ahmad and Al-Charu and Tirmidhi called it Hasan. This is a tradition of Hasan Basri from Samra and there is a difference in the hearing of Hasan Basri from Samra.) In the tradition of Abu Dawud and Nasa'i: \""Whoever castrates his slave"," We will castrate him.\"""""
"997","On the authority of Hazrat Umar, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: \The son will not be retaliated against the father.\"" (It was narrated by Ahmad"," Tirmidhi and Ibn Majah"," Ibn Jarood and Bayhaqi declared it authentic"," and Tirmidhi said that there is confusion in this hadith.)"""
"998","It was narrated from Hazrat Abu Juhaifa (RA) that I asked Hazrat Ali (RA): Do you people have anything other than the Qur'an revealed through revelation? He replied: No, by the One who grew the seed and created the soul! Except for the understanding that Allah gives to a person about the Qur'an and what is written in this scripture. I asked what is in this scripture? He said that the commandments of Dayt are the command to set a prisoner free and that no Muslim shall be killed in exchange for a disbeliever. And even the lowest of them can give Aman on their behalf. And they are a handful compared to the foreigners. And a believer will not be killed in exchange for an unbeliever, nor can a covenant (dhimmi) be killed during his covenant period."
"999","It is narrated from Hazrat Anas bin Malik that a slave girl was found in such a condition that her head was placed between two stones and crushed. People asked him who has done this to you? So and so? So and so? Even when he mentioned a Jew, he nodded: (Yes.) So the Jew was arrested, then he confessed. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered his head to be crushed between two stones. (Bukhari and Muslim. These words are from Muslim.)"
"1000","It was narrated from Hazrat Imran bin Hussain (may Allah be pleased with him) that a boy from the poor people cut off the ear of a boy from the rich people, so these (rich) people came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). You have not ordained anything for them. (Narrated by Ahmad and all three with a Sahih chain of transmission.)"
"1001","Hazrat Amr bin Shuaib narrated from his father and he narrated from his grandfather that a man pierced the knee of another with a horn. He came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Make me pay him. He said: \(No!) even if you are healed.\"" He then came to you and said: Give me retribution. You made him retaliate. After that he came to you again and said: O Messenger of Allah! I'm lame. He said: \""I forbade you but you disobeyed me.\"" May Allah remove you and your lameness is nullified.” Then the Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings of Allah be upon him"," forbade taking revenge for the injury before the injured person is healed. (This hadith has been narrated by Ahmad and Darqutni and is called Maaloool due to its transmission.)"""
"1002","It is narrated from Hazrat Abu Huraira (RA) that two women of the Huzail tribe fought with each other, and one of them hit the other with a stone and killed the woman and what was in her womb. So those people brought a dispute to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, decided that the birth of the fetus is Ghara, meaning a slave or a concubine. And declared the death of the (murderer) woman (by) her heirs. And the heirs of this (deity) were made the children of the deceased and other heirs along with them. Hamal bin Nabagha Hazli said: O Messenger of Allah! How can we pay for such a child who neither drank nor ate nor spoke nor screamed? That will be in vain. He said: \Because of this rhyming word"," which he said"," he seems to be among the brothers of the priests.\"" (Bukhari and Muslim). Hazrat Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that Hamal bin Nabagha stood up and narrated that I was between two women and one of them killed the other. (He narrated it briefly and Ibn Hibban and Hakim called it Sahih.)"""
"1003","It was narrated from Hazrat Anas that his paternal grandmother Rubai'a bint Nazr broke the front tooth of a girl. Rubai'a's relatives asked him for forgiveness, but the girls refused. Then he offered to give a dowry, but he rejected that too. So he came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, and refused to accept anything except Qisas. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered retribution. Hearing this, Hazrat Anas bin Nazr said: O Messenger of Allah! Will Rabi'a's tooth be broken? No, by the Most Holy One who has given you the truth and sent you! His tooth will not be broken. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “O Anas! Allah's decision is retribution.'' Then the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \There are some servants of Allah who"," if they swear by Allah"," Allah fulfills their oath.\"" (Bukhari and Muslim. And these words are Bukhari's)."""
"1004","On the authority of Hazrat Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \A person who is killed in a riot (so that his killer is not known) or is killed with a stone"," whip or stick in such a way that the killer is not aware"," then his death will be the death of murder.\"" And the person who will be killed intentionally is retribution. The curse of Allah is upon the person who prevents him from taking revenge.”"""
"1005","On the authority of Hazrat Ibn Umar, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \When a man captures a man and another kills the captured man"," the murderer will be killed and the capturer will be imprisoned.\"""""
"1006","It was narrated on the authority of Hazrat Abd al-Rahman bin Belmani that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, killed a Muslim in exchange for a covenant (dhimmi) and said: \I am closer to the person who fulfills his covenant.\"""""
"1007","It is narrated from Hazrat Ibn Umar that a slave was killed by deception, then Hazrat Umar said: If all the people of Sana'a had participated in his killing, I would have killed them all in return. (Narrated by Bukhari.)"
"1008","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Shureeh al-Khuza'i, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \After this sermon of mine"," if a man is killed"," his heirs have two options: either take the death or kill the murderer in exchange for the slain.\"""""
"1009","Abu Bakr bin Muhammad bin Amr bin Hazm narrates from his father (Muhammad) and he (Abu Bakr) from his grandfather (Amr bin Hazm) that the Prophet (peace be upon him) wrote to the people of Yemen. Then narrated a long hadith. There is also this in it: \Whoever kills an innocent Muslim and there is proof of this murder"," Qisas is obligatory upon him\"" unless the heirs of the deceased agree (to the deed). And the death of one soul is a hundred camels. And in the nose there is also full deity"," if it is cut off from the root. And for the two eyes"," the tongue"," and the two lips"," there is full deity. (Similarly) there is full deity in the organ specific. And the two testicles have a full diet. And in the back there is a whole day. And one foot has half a day. And a third is in the deep wound of the brain and stomach. And a wound that breaks a bone and dislodges it is worth fifteen camels. And there are ten camels in each finger and toe. And the value of one tooth is five camels. And in such a wound from which the bones are visible"," five camels are buried. And the man will be killed in exchange for the woman. And those who do not have (camels and) if they have gold"," they will be charged a thousand dinars.”"""
"1010","Hazrat Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “The death penalty for murder will be divided into five parts: twenty rights, twenty tribes, twenty daughters of Makhaz, twenty daughters of Lubun, and twenty Banu Lubun.” And Ibn Abi Shaybah has narrated it in another way, and it is more correct than Marfu'. And Abu Dawud and Tirmidhi have narrated it with authority on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib on the authority of Abiyyah on the authority of Jeddah: “Thirty rights in Dayt, thirty trunks and forty pregnant camels with babies in their bellies” (will be received.)"
"1011","Hazrat Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: “The people who disobey Allah the Most are of three types: (one) who kills in the Haram of Allah, (second) one who kills his non-slayer, and (third) one who kills because of the enmity of Jahiliyyah.”"
"1012","Hadhrat Abdullah bin Amr bin As, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \The death of a wrongful act"," i.e."," suspicion of intent"," which is done with a whip and a stick"," is a hundred camels.\"" Among them will be forty she-camels with babies in their bellies.” (Narrated by Abu Dawud"," Al-Nisa’i and Ibn Majah"," and Ibn Hibban said it to be Sahih.)"""
"1013","It is narrated from Hazrat Ibn Abbas, may God bless him and grant him peace, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “This and this”, that is, the ring finger and the thumb, are equal. Ten camels in return."
"1014","Hazrat Amr bin Shuaib has narrated from his father and he has narrated from his grandfather (Abdullah bin Amr bin As, may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The person who treated someone, even though he is not well-known in medicine, then kills someone or harms someone else, he will be held responsible.” This hadith has also been narrated by al-Bukhari and Muslim, but the one who has narrated this tradition as a messenger is more powerful than the narrators who have narrated it as received.)"
"1015","On the authority of Hazrat Abdullah bin Amr, the Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: \In those wounds in which the flesh is removed from the bone"," there are five camels (deat).\"" (This has been narrated by Imam Ahmad"," may God have mercy on him"," and all four others) and Imam Ahmad"," may God have mercy on him"," has narrated this addition: \""All the fingers are equal","\"" that is"," their deat is ten ten camels."""
"1016","On the authority of Hazrat Abdullah bin Amr, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The diet of the dhimmis is half of the diet of the Muslims.” (Narrated by Ahmad and the four). Khazima declared it to be correct.)"
"1017","It was narrated from him (Abdullah ibn Amr, may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \The death of a suspected murder is as bad as a murder of intent.\"" But the (suspected) murderer will not be killed. That (suspicious intention) is such that Satan jumps (among people) (and incites and incites them to murder) as a result of which blood is spoiled without any enmity or taking up arms."""
"1018","It was narrated from Hazrat Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) that during the reign of the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) a man killed another man, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fixed his death penalty at twelve thousand (dirhams). (Narrated by all four of them. Ornasai and Abu Hatim preferred the transmission of this tradition.)"
"1019","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Ramtha, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I attended the service of the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, while my son was with me. He inquired: \Who is this?\"" I said: It is my son. I (openly) say this. He said: \""Indeed"," you are not responsible for his crime"," nor is he responsible for your crime.\"""""
"1020","Hazrat Sahl bin Abu Hatmah narrates from some of the elders of his people that Abdullah bin Sahl and Hazrat Muhaissa bin Masoud (RA) left for Khyber because of their poverty. Muhaisa (RA) came to the Jews and said: By Allah! You guys killed him. He said: By Allah! We did not kill him. Then Muhaisa and her brother Huwaysa and Abd al-Rahman bin Sahl (may God be pleased with them) all three came (to the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace), and Muhaisa wanted to speak, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Let the elder speak and consider his right.\"" \""You meant that the one who is older among you should speak.\"" So Hawaisah spoke. Then Muhaisah spoke"," and the Messenger of Allah"," may God's prayers and peace be upon him"," said: \""They will either pay the death of your master and companion or declare war.\"" Then he wrote a letter to him in this regard"," to which he wrote: By Allah! We did not kill him. Then the Messenger of Allah"," may God bless him and grant him peace"," said to Huwaysa"," Muhaissa and Abd al-Rahman bin Sahl"," may God be pleased with them: \""Will you swear an oath and be entitled to the blood of your master?\"" They said: No. He said: \""Then the Jews swear to you?\"" He said that they are not Muslims (therefore their oath is not valid). ) So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave him (Abdullah bin Sahl radi Allahu anhu) the diet from his own (Bait al-Mal) and sent a hundred camels to him. Hazrat Sahl (may Allah be pleased with him) said that one of them"," a red colored camel"," kicked me. (Bukhari and Muslim)."""
"1021","It is narrated from an Ansari Companion that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, maintained the method of Qasamat of the Jahiliyyah. And you accordingly judged a slain among some of the Ansar whom they claimed against the Jews. (Narrated by Muslim.)"
"1022","On the authority of Hazrat Abdullah bin Umar, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \He who takes up arms against us is not one of us.\"" (Bukhari and Muslim)"""
"1023","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Hurairah, the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: “Whoever goes out of obedience (to the Imam) and separates from the Muslim community and dies in that state, then his death will be the death of Jahiliyyah.” (Narrated by Muslim)."
"1024","It is narrated on the authority of Umm Salamah (RA) that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: “Hazrat Ammar (RA) will be killed by a rebel group.” (Narrated by Muslim)"
"1025","On the authority of Hazrat Abdullah bin Umar, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O son of Umm Abd! Do you know what is Allah's decision regarding the rebels of this nation?\ He said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: \""His wounded will not be tortured"," nor his captives will be killed"," nor will the fugitive be chased"," nor will his property be divided as booty.\"" It is proven. (Narrated by Ibn Abi Shaiba and al-Hakim.)"""
"1026","Hazrat Arfaja bin Shareeh says that I heard the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: \Whoever comes to you while you are all united and wants to create division in your congregation"," then kill him.\"" (Narrated by Muslim)."""
"1027","On the authority of Hazrat Abdullah bin Umar, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Whoever is killed while protecting his wealth is a martyr.\"""""
"1028","It was narrated from Imran bin Hussain that Hazrat Yala bin Umayyah had a fight with a person. When one of them bit the other with his teeth, he pulled his hand from his mouth and pulled it out, so that his front tooth broke and fell out. Then both of them took their dispute to the court of the Prophet, peace be upon him, and he said: \Does one of you bite his brother like a camel?\"" There is no religion for him.” (Bukhari and Muslim. And these words are from Muslim)."""
"1029","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Huraira, may God bless him and grant him peace, Abu al-Qasim, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \If a man peeps into your house without permission and you throw a stone at his eye"," then there is no sin on you.\"" (Bukhari and Muslim)."""
"1030","It is narrated on the authority of Hazrat Bara bin Azib that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, decided that the protection and supervision of gardens during the day is the responsibility of the owners of the garden. And the protection and supervision of the cattle at night is the responsibility of the cattle owners. And the amount of damage caused by the cattle during the night is on the owners of the cattle. (This hadith has been narrated by all four except Ahmad and Tirmidhi and Ibn Hibban has called it Sahih, but there is a difference in its chain of transmission.)"
"1031","It was narrated from Hazrat Mu'adh bin Jabal (RA) about a person who first converted to Islam and then became a Jew, \I will not sit until he is killed.\"" This is the decision of Allah and His Messenger (peace be upon him). Then ordered to kill him and he was killed. (Bukhari and Muslim) and in a hadith of Abu Dawud: He was asked to repent before the killing."""
"1032","On the authority of Hazrat Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Kill him who changes his religion.\"" (Narrated by Bukhari)."""
"1033","It was narrated from Hazrat Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, that a blind man had a concubine who used to abuse and speak ill of the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace. Those blind companions used to forbid her, but she would not stop. One night, they took a hoe and put it on his stomach and pressed it with their load and killed him. This matter reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he said: “Beware! You be the witness! His blood went in vain and in vain."
